    {
      "id": "ko-plain-c1-001",
      "level": "C1",
      "sourceSha256": "8f87b38d0f1f582c2434dfea01d65c88ed64bcbf19c9f2c5121d772322bbd3df",
      "lines": [
        {
          "index": 1,
          "text": "언어 학습 모임에서 피드백은 정확성을 높이는 데 필요하지만, 그 시점과 방식에 따라 참여를 위축시킬 수도 있어요.",
          "meaning": "In a language-learning group, feedback is needed to improve accuracy, but its timing and form can also discourage participation.",
          "speechSeconds": 11.275,
          "audio": "https://audio.talktag.co.kr/Korean/audio-essays-articles/segments-001/v1-20261016/c1/line-01.mp3?v=351079619545",
          "sha256": "3510796195455e12b12eb2b0d2d14d19762ecfb11bf9e30bf7a1dc497953ad50",
          "bytes": 116565
        },
        {
          "index": 2,
          "text": "발화가 진행되는 동안 작은 오류를 모두 바로잡으면 학습자는 자신의 메시지보다 실수에 더 집중하게 돼요.",
          "meaning": "If every small error is corrected while someone is speaking, learners focus more on mistakes than on their message.",
          "speechSeconds": 10.67,
          "audio": "https://audio.talktag.co.kr/Korean/audio-essays-articles/segments-001/v1-20261016/c1/line-02.mp3?v=20a35d542bf6",
          "sha256": "20a35d542bf6f6a95cf852f1fb1537308bf381b336d5f2c9e340619019cd4b9a",
          "bytes": 109605
        },
        {
          "index": 3,
          "text": "반면 의미 전달이 끝난 뒤, 학습자가 요청한 한두 가지 항목에만 피드백을 제공하면 다음 시도에 적용하기가 훨씬 쉬워져요.",
          "meaning": "By contrast, after the meaning has been communicated, giving feedback on only one or two points the learner has requested is much easier to apply in the next attempt.",
          "speechSeconds": 13.11,
          "audio": "https://audio.talktag.co.kr/Korean/audio-essays-articles/segments-001/v1-20261016/c1/line-03.mp3?v=7d938404db53",
          "sha256": "7d938404db53af70793b517d911040626486b6cc746bdae6b3bb223e7faef702",
          "bytes": 134877
        },
        {
          "index": 4,
          "text": "따라서 효과적인 진행자는 오류를 발견하는 사람이라기보다, 언제 무엇을 다룰지 판단하는 사람에 가까워요.",
          "meaning": "An effective facilitator is therefore less someone who spots errors than someone who judges what to address and when.",
          "speechSeconds": 13.92,
          "audio": "https://audio.talktag.co.kr/Korean/audio-essays-articles/segments-001/v1-20261016/c1/line-04.mp3?v=7c685173d872",
          "sha256": "7c685173d8728e1ce3423c1b5724d744733af8b57e9351c8545b416a8625bdad",
          "bytes": 142389
        }
      ],
